From 180fabb41bdece45d48721ce49818ec9fc078994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:55:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/38] kebab: XNU-002a-2 append-only UniXNU boot entry (drop
 official UniXNUDxe)

The official UniXNUDxe puts its option FIRST in BootOrder, which would
displace the Project Silicium default. Gate 1 (manual boot-from-file) is
not available: neither UiApp nor BootManagerMenuApp is packed in this
firmware, so nothing offers 'Boot From File'.

Instead, XnuBootEntryDxe appends a Boot#### for the UniXNU application:
  - finds the FV that holds FILE_GUID 9B665204-... via Fv->ReadFile
  - builds <FV device path> + PIWG firmware-file node (subtype 0x06)
  - writes a load option whose optional data is 'unixnu:firmware'
  - appends the number to BootOrder ONLY if absent; default entry untouched
  - never touches BootNext and never reorders

The menu is built from exactly such FV-file boot options
(MsBootOptionsLib.c:246-248 registers Internal Storage / USB Storage /
FFU Mode the same way), so 'UniXNU' appears in the existing list.

UniXNUDxe.efi is no longer packed (the file stays in the repo, unused).
